Committed c3e09034f8137eeba6b6c5e715499c3fe745ba59.

Ownership decomposition:
- retained as Cellerator reusable math: non-owning device query, ANN-list, dense/Blocked-ELL/sliced-ELL index, result, and workspace views; explicit capacities; runtime probe/K contracts bounded at 32; caller stream; four-warp V100 probe and refine kernels; full cell/embryo/shard identity output; exact routed search remains in the separate exact_search owner.
- moved out of Cellerator ownership by removal: durable record accumulation and index building, CPU hash cell lookup, latent normalization and ordering policy, shard construction, device selection/residency/pooling, hidden allocation and transfers, device-wide synchronization, query-by-cell construction, and owning application results. Those belong to CellShard/BioPrep/application layers according to their storage, policy, and durable-result roles.
- consolidated the useful private ANN/fixed-K kernels into forward_neighbors.cu; deleted only duplicate orphaned .cuh fragments after preservation in the owning implementation. Obsolete duplicate exact kernels were removed because routed exact math remains in src/compute/neighbors/exact_search.

Boundary and allocation audit:
- no CellShard/cellshard symbols or includes in the owned forward-neighbor paths;
- no owning STL/host_array/device_buffer/shared_ptr/unique_ptr;
- no cudaMalloc/cudaFree/cudaMemcpy/cudaDeviceSynchronize;
- probe and refine remain device-resident and asynchronous on the caller stream.
- integration follow-up outside scope: remove stale CellShard::runtime target link in src/compute/current_targets.cmake and update docs/compute_and_models.qmd caller-surface wording.

Validation on Tesla V100-SXM2-16GB sm_70, driver 580.173.02, NVCC 12.9.86, Release -O3:
- direct target-equivalent compile passed;
- independent dense/Blocked-ELL/sliced-ELL equivalence test on a non-default stream passed exact cell ordering and insufficient-capacity rejection;
- Compute Sanitizer 12.9 memcheck passed, ERROR SUMMARY: 0 errors, under benchmark mutex;
- ptxas: all kernels report 0 spill stores/loads. Dense refine capacity 1/16/32: REG 40/48/48, STACK 24/384/768 bytes, SHARED 96/1536/3072 bytes per 128-thread block. Blocked maximum REG 56; sliced maximum REG 48. Probe capacity 8: REG 60, STACK 0, SHARED 256; capacity 16/32: REG 40, STACK 128/256, SHARED 512/1024.
- inferred sm_70 occupancy from register/block limits for K15 dense refine is 10 x 128-thread blocks = 62.5%; shared memory is not limiting.
- mutex-protected CUDA-event resident benchmark: 256 queries, 4096 index rows, 64 lists, dim 32, fp16 score/fp32 accumulate, probe 8, K15, 5 warmups, 21 repeats: median 0.328704 ms, min 0.326656, max 0.331776; two launches; explicit 8192-byte workspace and 122880-byte result capacity; steady H2D=0 and D2H=0.
- git diff --check passed and worktree clean.

The contract-split full CMake generation retains the already-recorded hard-coded ../CellShard test path limitation; direct target-equivalent build and all required CUDA validation completed.

Committed 182ccdf8fd89a35007aa5f7a5b8cd46e3433d6ba. Runtime-K raw-view public API and ordering preserved. Internal capacity classes 1,2,4,8,16,32 accept arbitrary K through the smallest containing class. Routed private/shared identity omits only kernel-constant shard_index; public result and cross-shard merge retain full int64 identities and tie ordering.

Tesla V100-SXM2-16GB sm_70, driver 580.173.02, NVCC 12.9.86, Release -O3 evidence:
- direct exactSearchRuntimeTest passed;
- Compute Sanitizer 12.9 memcheck: 0 errors under benchmark mutex;
- baseline routed: REG 44, STACK 1024, SHARED 1024, 0 spills; baseline merge REG 34, STACK 1024, 0 spills;
- candidate routed capacity 1/2/4/8/16/32 STACK+SHARED 24/48/96/192/384/768 bytes, REG 40-48, 0 spills;
- candidate merge STACK 32/64/128/256/512/1024, REG 28-34, SHARED 0, 0 spills;
- mutex-protected CUDA-event benchmark (256 queries, 4096 index rows, dim 32, fp16/fp32, 5 warmups, 21 repeats): baseline->candidate K1 0.434176->0.336896 ms, K15 1.198080->0.976896 ms, K32 5.322752->3.457024 ms;
- full-result checksums matched baseline at K 1,2,3,4,7,8,15,16,17,31,32;
- git diff --check passed and worktree clean.

Full CMake generation in the contract-split worktree hit pre-existing tests/CMakeLists.txt hard-coded ../CellShard paths. Direct target-equivalent compilation, runtime correctness, sanitizer, ptxas/cuobjdump, and V100 latency validation all completed.

